On 1/30/07, Pierre Abbat <phma@phma.optus.nu> wrote:
> On Tuesday 30 January 2007 16:22, Cortesi wrote:
>
> >  no xunpre ka'e du'i plipe
>
> {ka'e du'i plipe} is ungrammatical. {ka'e plipe du'i} or {du'iku ka'e plipe}.

Actually, {ka'e du'i plipe} is equivalent to {ka'e ku du'i plipe}.

The rules for compound tags are quite weird, but since {ku} is elidable
after a tag, they can usually be ignored.

